cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "CELL-NET: A Cellular Automaton Engine on an FPGA"
abstract: >-
  A cellular automaton engine in which every cell is its own logic circuit
  on a Gowin GW2A-18 FPGA and the whole grid updates on one clock edge. The
  repository includes the Verilog design and its cocotb test benches, a
  multithreaded C++20 engine with a written correctness proof and an
  exhaustive thread-schedule check, and measured throughput and latency
  for a laptop against the FPGA. FPGA timing figures come from cycle-accurate
  simulation of the complete chip.
type: software
